item: defect-1-viewport-rect-platform
class: SCENE
claim: Input::viewportRect exposes the rect plus the window size it was captured at, so stale-rect regression is a pure unit test with no GL context, and Window keeps it current through both size callbacks (the fix for 'orbit broken after maximise/fullscreen')
residue: covers the PURE logic only — setViewportRect, viewportRect, rectIsStaleFor, cursorOverViewport hit-testing. It does NOT prove the GLFW callbacks fire on a real resize (that is app.smoke_size_agree's mid-run EMBER_SMOKE_RESIZE), nor the D29 area-relay case where the rect is a sub-window area rather than the whole window (not landed; the whole-window assumption in these tests dies with it)
symbol: viewportRect
symbol_file: src/platform/Input.h
test: test_platform_input
test_file: tests/test_platform_input.cpp
